case or all keys are strings in upper case, else return false.
The function should return false is the given associative array is empty.
Examples:
>>> check_dict_case(["a": "apple", "b": "banana"].nullable)
true
>>> check_dict_case(["a": "apple", "A": "banana", "B": "banana"].nullable)
